What is Git?
Git is a Version Control System


git init : initialize an empty repository
git status : gives the information of the current state of the git repository
git checkout -b 'branch name' : Switching to new branch if you want to switch to an existing branch then use git checkout branch with -b
git add 'file name' : used to staged the untracked files
git branch : gives the info / list of all the branches in git repo
git commit -m "message" : to commit the files into git / used to track the staged files after being added by git add
git remote -v : to check the remote repo
git fetch : to update the git
git pull : to update the local repo and pull from the remote repo
git log : to check the commits and logs
git log --oneline : to check the logs in oneline
git branch 'name' : to create a new branch
git branch -r : to check the branches on remote
git switch 'name' : to switch to the new branch
git switch -c 'name' : to create a new branch and switch to the new branch
git push origin 'name' : to push the branches from local to remote
git branch -d 'name' : to delete the branch from the local repo
git push origin --delete 'name' : to delete the branches from the remote repo
git merge 'name' : to merge the branch in main branch with history
git rebase 'name' : to merge the branch in main branch without history
git diff 'name' : to check the difference of branches


. Git Stash & Pop

git stash -u : to keep the file in the shelf, so we can work on other file
git stash list : to list all the stash files
git stash pop : to bring back the stash files
git stash save "Message" : to add the files in stash after git add
git stash pop "stash id" : to bring back the specific stash file


. Git Cherry Pick 

First we need to switch to the main branch

git cherry-pick "commit id" : to merge a specific file from other branch to main branch
git cherry-pick "first commit id"^"last commit id" : to merge the multiple files from other branch to main branch


. Git Tags

git tag "tag name v.1.2" : to tag the latest commit
git tag : to list the tags
git push origin "tag name" : to push the tag from local to remote repo
git tag -a "tag name -m" "message" : to push the tag from local to remote repo
git tag -a "tag name" commit id -m "message" : to push a specific tag to the remote repo
git tag -d "tag name" : to delete the tag from local
git push origin --delete "tag name" : to delete the tags from the remote repo


. Git Squash

git rebase -i HEAD~5 : to merge multiple commits into single commit
                     : in terminal need to replace the pick to s/squash and first commit will remain pick as we need to combined the commits into first commit
		     : then we need to write a message for the commit
git commit --amend : to modify the latest commit message
git rebase -i HEDA~5 : to modify the commit message for specific commit
                     : in terminal which commit message need to change update the message before commit id and save
		     : in new terminal change/update the message it will save
git push --force : to push the change on the remote repo


. Git Revert

git revert "commit id" : to revert the changes
                       : in terminal provide a message
                       : an extra commit will be added to maintain history


. Git Reset

there are 3 modes of reset --hard reset, --mixed reset, --soft reset

- Hard Reset

git reset "file name" : to remove the file from staging area
git reset --hard : to remove all the files from the staging & delete
git reset --hard HEAD~2 : to remove or delete the commits and point head to the mentioned commit id 
git reset --hard "commit id" : to remove or delete commits and point head to the mentioned commit id
git push origin main --force : to push the changes forcefully to remote repo

- Mixed Reset

git reset --mixed HEAD~1 : to move the head and the file will be move from commit to work directory
git reset --mixed "commit id" : to move the head and remove the files from commit and add them to work directory
git push --force : to push the changes to remote repo

- Soft Reset

git reset --soft HEAD~1 : to move the head and modify the commit message and move the file to staging area
git reset --soft "commit id" : to move the head and modify the commit message and move the file to staging area
git reset --soft "commit id" : to combined the commits in one go 
git push origin main --force : to push the changes to remote repo


. Git Ignore

first create a .gitignore file to apply the rule

eg: 
    build/
    *.env
    *.log
    *.txt : to ignore this extension files to push on repo

then we need add the files in staging area using git add, then you can see only files without this extension they will be ignore by git   

